      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thinking about this some more.\n\nWhat we\u0027re trying to test is what happens if an app without the permission tries to start a VM.\n\nAnd actually the answer is, it crashes horribly rather than returning a permission failure.\n\nWe can rework the test, as here, to avoid that crash. But a 3P app would see the same crash.\n\nSo I wonder if we should instead make sure that we map the exec failure to a better error, making it clear to the caller what the problem is? And just directly return a permission denied / security exception?\n\n@davidai@google.com @ioffe@google.com fyi",
      "revId": "d658c51732e3691f0a5c5b29562044cf40751dff",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
