      "writtenOn": "2024-04-03T01:18:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e However, isRemoteAttestationSupported() and isUpdatableVmSupported() do require the permission, and that\u0027s part of the API definition, and we\u0027re no longer allowed to change it.\n\nThanks, now I got the key. Though the situation `isFeatureEnabled` requires the permission but not for `getSupportedOsList` seems weird, we cannot change anything since they\u0027re defined as API specification.\n\nThen what I should do from now looks quite straightforward. In Java code, I should implement checking whether `vendor_module` feature is enabled or not w/o relying on `virtmgr`.",
      "parentUuid": "3b2589b5_85120931",
      "revId": "d658c51732e3691f0a5c5b29562044cf40751dff",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
